==Trivia==
*In the Enigma Stages tutorial, [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] are called "legendary Cats" ("Legend Cats" pre-[[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]]).
*The actual method of players upgrading their Enigma Level is to unlock certain [[Meow Medals]]. Hence, completing the corresponding stages is not what increases players' Enigma Levels; players have to '''obtain''' the relevant units in order to meet the requirements.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]], [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Master of Life Dr. Nova]] and Mythic Cats from Zero Legends are the only drop units from the main [[Legend Stages]] who don't increase the player's Enigma Level.
*Enigma Level 6 was added in [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]] alongside [[Hunter's Map I|Hunter's Maps I]], [[Hunter's Map II|II]] and [[Hunter's Map III|III]].
**Enigma Levels 7 ~ 9 were added in [[Version 12.0 Update|Version 12.0]].
**Enigma Level 10 was added in [[Version 12.4 Update|Version 12.4]] alongside [[Hunter's Map IV]].
*Although the first image for the Enigma Stage tutorial includes a platinum Enigma, no such item can be found in-game.
*Sprites for two more Enigma rarities can be found in the game's files.
**[[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]] implemented the first of the two unused types, Illusory Maps, along with very slightly changing its color.
*[[An Hour's Training (Insane)|Shack of Spirit]], [[A Month's Training (Deadly)|Cave of Spirit]] and [[A Year's Training (Deadly)|Labyrinth of Spirit]] all reference the [[wikia:dragonball:Hyperbolic Time Chamber|Room of Spirit and Time]] from ''Dragon Ball''. The reference is more obvious with the maps' Japanese names.
*[[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Aku|Bad Instinct's Origin]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Aku|Bad Instinct's Apex]] and [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Aku|Bad Instinct's Refuge]] are the only Talent Orb Enigma maps not to follow the "Cradle, Summit, Frontier" naming scheme.
*[[Hunter's Map IV]] is the only Enigma map to introduce a new enemy.
*While the Japanese name of Enigma Stages (発掘ステージ ''Hakkutsu Sutēji'') can be translated as "Excavation Stages", it isn't the same as the [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!]] [[Gauntlet]]'s [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Excavation Lv.1~20|Excavation Lvs.]] (出土Lvs. ''Shutsudo Lvs.''). The Enigma Stages use the term 発掘, which means discovering something via excavation, whereas 出土 has the connotation of being unearthed and taken from the ground.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], [[Dark Cradle]], [[Dark Summit]] and [[Dark Frontier]] were named Black Cradle, Black Summit and Black Frontier, respectively.

